  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Wednesday) \nIssued at 1022 PM CDT Tue Oct 27 2026\n\nOf course, anyone reading this is wondering about the weekend rain. \nIt's safe to say, we're gonna get it. The question is when. When I \nleft here last Friday, the GFS already had two days in the books \nbringing rain in here Saturday evening. 4 days later, that hasn't \nchanged, so there has been some serious consistency with this. In \nthe same vain, the Euro was dry all weekend. As of the 12Z run, it \nlooks like it's finally coming around to the GFS, however just not \nas early. It's leaning more toward after midnight arrival. The NBM \nrefuses to take a stand one way or the other, so we're gonna be \nanother day or two to work the trick-or-treating news. The good news \nis forecast soundings aren't looking thundery. Unfortunately, this \nisn't going to be anything near a drought buster as most, if not all \nof Middle TN, will register less than 1 inch.\n\nHere's the best news: the arrival of this weekend's rains looks to \nbe a shift in the overall pattern with more rain in the cards next \nweek.",
